{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'find /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/resources -maxdepth 3 -type f; cat /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/workflow/observations.py | head -105; cat /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/resources/tasks/audit.md'","aggregated_output":"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/resources/tasks/audit.md\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/resources/skills/consensus-analysis/SKILL.md\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/resources/skills/evidence-review/SKILL.md\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/resources/__pycache__/__init__.cpython-310.pyc\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/resources/system.md\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/resources/__init__.py\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src/consensus_assurance/resources/task-skills.json\n\"\"\"Finite, non-evaluating event correlation and fully observed safety monitors.\"\"\"\nfrom consensus_assurance.core.types import Comparison\nfrom consensus_assurance.core.events import MISSING, field, compare, match_prerequisites, event_requirements\n\n\ndef compare_events(events, comparison, requirements, comparison_index=0):\n    \"\"\"Keep existential witnesses separate from completeness of the observed scope.\"\"\"\n    results, missing, correlations, outside, diagnostics = [], [], {}, [], []\n    admission = None\n    admission_dependencies = []\n    admission_error = ''\n    if requirements:\n        try:\n            declared = event_requirements(requirements)\n            admission = next((r for r in declared if r.alias == comparison.admission_alias), None)\n            if admission is None or any(r.event==comparison.event for r in declared):\n                admission_error = 'Explicit admission_alias is missing or prerequisites depend on the result'\n            else:\n                wanted={c.reference.partition('.')[0] for c in admission.conditions if c.reference}\n                for req in reversed(declared):\n                    if req.alias in wanted:wanted.update(c.reference.partition('.')[0] for c in req.conditions if c.reference)\n                admission_dependencies=[r for r in declared if r.alias in wanted]\n        except ValueError as exc:\n            admission_error = str(exc)\n    def gap(index, reason):\n        missing.append(index)\n        diagnostics.append({'event_index':index, 'identity':{k:field(events[index],k)\n            for k in comparison.identity_fields if field(events[index],k) is not MISSING}, 'reason':reason})\n    for index, event in enumerate(events):\n        if event.get('event') != comparison.event:\n            continue\n        independent = [c for c in comparison.applicability_conditions if not c.reference]\n        if any(compare(event,c) is False for c in independent):\n            outside.append(index)\n            continue\n        absent = [k for k in comparison.identity_fields if field(event,k) is MISSING]\n        absent += [c.field for c in independent if compare(event,c) is None]\n        if absent:\n            gap(index, 'Missing identity or applicability fields: '+', '.join(dict.fromkeys(absent)))\n            continue\n        aliases = {}\n        if requirements is not None:\n            linked = match_prerequisites(events, requirements, index, comparison.identity_fields)\n            correlations[str(index)] = linked\n            if linked['status'] != 'matched':\n                gap(index, linked['reason'])\n                continue\n            aliases = {alias:events[i] for alias,i in linked['alias_indices'].items()}\n        applicability = [compare(event,c,aliases) for c in comparison.applicability_conditions if c.reference]\n        if any(value is False for value in applicability):\n            outside.append(index)\n            continue\n        if any(value is None for value in applicability):\n            gap(index, 'Missing alias-dependent applicability fields')\n            continue\n        value = compare(event,comparison.assertion,aliases)\n        if comparison.antecedent is not None:\n            antecedent = compare(event,comparison.antecedent,aliases) if comparison.antecedent else None\n            value = None if antecedent is None or value is None else not antecedent or value\n        if value is None:\n            gap(index, 'Missing required result fields: '+comparison.assertion.field+\n                (' or '+comparison.antecedent.field if comparison.antecedent else ''))\n        else:\n            results.append((index,value))\n    violations = [index for index,value in results if value is False]\n    # A missing result in the same operation can affect its witness. Unknown\n    # identity is not evidence of independence; distinct runner streams are.\n    def independent_operation(left, right):\n        a, b = events[left], events[right]\n        if a.get('_ca_stream') is not None and b.get('_ca_stream') is not None and a['_ca_stream'] != b['_ca_stream']:\n            return True\n        return any(field(a,k) is not MISSING and field(b,k) is not MISSING\n            and compare(a, Comparison(field=k,reference='other.'+k), {'other':b}) is False\n            for k in comparison.identity_fields)\n    if admission and not admission_error:\n        for index,event in enumerate(events):\n            if event.get('event') != admission.event:continue\n            if any(compare(event,c) is False for c in admission.conditions if not c.reference):continue\n            aliases={}\n            if admission_dependencies:\n                linked=match_prerequisites(events,admission_dependencies,index,comparison.identity_fields)\n                if linked['status']!='matched':\n                    gap(index,'Operation admission history: '+linked['reason'])\n                    continue\n                aliases={alias:events[i] for alias,i in linked['alias_indices'].items()}\n            checks=[compare(event,c,aliases) for c in admission.conditions]\n            if any(v is False for v in checks):continue\n            if any(v is None for v in checks) or any(field(event,k) is MISSING for k in comparison.identity_fields):\n                gap(index, 'Missing operation admission fields or identity')\n                continue\n            if not any(r>index and event.get('_ca_stream')==events[r].get('_ca_stream') and\n                    all(field(event,k) is not MISSING and compare(event,Comparison(field=k,reference='result.'+k),{'result':events[r]}) is True for k in comparison.identity_fields)\n                    and (r in outside or correlations.get(str(r),{}).get('alias_indices',{}).get(admission.alias)==index)\n                    for r in [i for i,_ in results]+outside):\n                gap(index, 'Admitted operation has no complete applicable result observation')\n    valid = [index for index in violations if not admission_error and all(independent_operation(index,m) for m in missing)]\n    complete = bool(results) and not missing and not admission_error\n    limitations = [f\"Event {d['event_index']} {d['identity']}: {d['reason']}\" for d in diagnostics]\n    if admission_error:limitations.append(admission_error)\n    if not results and not missing:\n        limitations.append('No applicable completed result event was reached')\n    return {'comparison_index':comparison_index,\n        'outcome':'violated' if valid else 'unknown' if missing or not results or admission_error else 'holds',\n        'witness_indices':violations, 'valid_witness_indices':valid, 'witness_complete':bool(valid),\n        'comparison_complete':complete, 'missing_indices':sorted(set(missing)),\n# One file-backed update\n\nRead research.json for source/draft paths, questions, actual results and locators, necessary gaps, changed knowledge, backend/build inputs and allocation. Detailed history lives in state.json and referenced receipts. Start with the small update example; consult only needed $defs in submission.schema.json, not the whole schema.\n\nWrite JSON in draft and return its relative path plus a short summary. Optional validation.command checks those bytes read-only and reserves no capacity. Acceptance reads retained bytes. Rejected whole drafts and diagnostics return for ordinary repair in this session; editable drafts never override receipts.\n\nThe envelope requires rationale; sources, investigations, knowledge, gaps, interpretations, experiment and stop are optional. Existing records use explicit IDs. Unique @names may refer to new questions/knowledge within a batch. The controller assigns IDs, revisions and comparison indices. Source IDs identify acquired file/ranges; do not create aliases merely to count handoffs.\n\n- investigations: create a sourced question or update specified fields of id. Hypothesis/discriminator may be provisional. parent_id links a child without closing its parent. paused needs resume_conditions; explained/closed retain unresolved boundaries and grounded interpretations.\n- knowledge: behavior/fact statement, conditions and sources, optionally execution indices. Correct an existing id using changed_premise and affected_uses from recorded dependencies. References specify entry_id/revision and optionally the assertion used. Old bases remain available.\n- gaps: necessary question under investigation_id; optional experiment_id limits it to that experiment and successors. Put broader directions in discriminator or limitations. answers maps exact gap IDs to sourced/observed explanations. Identical updates do not duplicate gaps.\n- interpretations: investigation_id, optional experiment_id, source_ids, rationale and conclusion (explained, conditional, violated, holds, unresolved). executions maps target receipt IDs to decisive parsed indices; an experiment interpretation needs its own receipt. Separate producer receipts need joint_history. Unresolved/conditional accounts may retain failed receipts with no decisive events. Preserve knowledge uses, counterevidence and limitations. Optional report_title/report_answer are Chinese presentation, never verdicts.\n- experiment: one invocation with investigation_id, harness_path, optional files (workspace destination → draft path), source_ids, scope and prefix, including supplied assumptions. requirement/responsibility and comparisons are optional; requirements need verified source anchors, which do not prove source meaning. A comparison owns event, identity_fields, admission_alias, assertion and optional antecedent/applicability_conditions. prerequisites use explicit alias dependencies, not array order. Cases/controls can share execution. Changed basis uses previous_id/revision_reason and receives fresh execution.\n- stop: bounded_completed only for a preconfigured finite directed task with no necessary unfinished work. Cancellation, service refusal, permission loss and exhausted resources are controller boundaries, not model declarations.\n\nGo execution_package selects one captured local package; Rust selects a crate and tests/<basename>.rs; Python has no package override. Follow backend instructions for protected source, dependencies, locks, features, support and caches. Exploration and specified checks use identical fixed-input isolation. Agent shell networking is disabled; executor communication is confined to its private namespace.\n\nExact unchanged updates receive no_change, retained raw cost and useful current work, without duplicate semantic revisions or automatic stopping. Turn allocation and its CheckRun establish timing; preflight elapsed time is a checkpoint. Expiry requires no closing submission.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
